#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:13
msgid "Custom SCons command-line options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:15
msgid ""
"PlatformIO is built on top of the open-source software construction tool "
"called SCons. SCons has many useful command-line options that control its "
"behavior and may come in handy to know the exact internal processes "
"happening in SCons when it builds a target. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:20
msgid ""
"``--dry-run`` configures SCons to print the commands that would be executed "
"to build any target, but do not execute the commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:22
msgid ""
"``--tree=all`` forces SCons to print file dependency tree including implicit "
"and ignored dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:24
msgid ""
"``--debug=explain`` will print an explanation of why SCons decides to "
"(re-)build the targets it selects for building."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:27
msgid ""
"The list of available command-line options can be found in the official "
"`SCons documentation <https://scons.org/doc/production/HTML/scons-user/ch10."
"html#sect-command-line-options>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/custom-scons-cli-options.rst:30
msgid ""
"The easiest way to pass extra command-line options to the SCons build system "
"used in PlatformIO is via the external ``SCONSFLAGS`` environment variable:"
msgstr ""
